{"ref":"BDB, עַרְבִי","hw":"עַרְבִי","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">עַרְבִי</span></big>  <strong>adj.gent. Arabian (</strong>in strictly ethnographic sense, Nö<sup>l.c.</sup><strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">הָע׳</span> as subst. <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 2:19\" href=\"/Nehemiah.2.19\">Ne 2:19</a> Geshem <em>the Arabian</em>, so <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 6:1\" href=\"/Nehemiah.6.1\">6:1</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">הָעַרְבִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 4:1\" href=\"/Nehemiah.4.1\">Ne 4:1</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 21:16\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.21.16\">2 Ch 21:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 22:1\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.22.1\">22:1</a>; also (written as NH) <span dir=\"rtl\">הערביים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 26:7\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.26.7\">26:7</a> (Qr <span dir=\"rtl\">הָעַרְבִים</span>), and even <span dir=\"rtl\">הָעַרְבִיאִים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 17:11\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.17.11\">17:11</a>.","next":"BDB, עֲרָבָה","prev":"BDB, עֲרָב"}